/-!
# Operational and OSLF meaning of the shared judgment services

The actual submitted service request produces its actual indexed response.
A successful response binds its native payload in the authored scoped body.
Completion then requires a step of the authored effect-tree LanguageDef; it
is not defined as the graph of the reference world evaluator. A third step
emits a precise occurrence from that complete ordered list.

The resulting OSLF observation preserves the request, response, native value,
branch, state and deferred intents. Decline remains an observable response
without a continuation. HOL proof acceptance still means source derivability
and formation of its native representation, not native proof inhabitation.

This is an internal typed request protocol with a compiled effect backend.
It is not a codec for external HOL proof bytes or a textual language frontend.
Its finite continuation semantics does not establish termination of general
proof search or completeness of arbitrary OSLF formula checking.
-/

